 only get cover up to July 2026 figures in the approved budget. It strikes me that – at the very least- it makes it much more likely we will have a real fight with Ds about security this time, and the point about revisiting ATE post-PDD Trial outcome seemed
 to get very little traction with Cockerill when we raised it at the PTR in an attempt to get the hearing of any applications pushed back. The potential prejudice to Ds is that, if we don’t get the additional cover they say we may need, it would be late September/start
 of October before they’d be able to get a SFC hearing listed, at which point we are into the T3 Trial. So it’s not so much about how much of T3/G2’s costs have been incurred by the time the PDD Judgment is out, it is how much has been incurred once we’ve got
 to a hearing that has only been listed once the judgment has come out. I got the impression at the PTR when considering the timetable that that was what Cockerill was concerned about, and she was keen to deal with T3/G2 security once and for all in January.

