mber of areas where it would be helpful for Alicia to provide some more information in this statement. I understand the sensitivities surrounding these areas, but in circumstances where the court is very likely to ask these questions, it is far better to have something in a witness statement rather than have to give an answer on instructions in court.&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; First, we need to provide the court with some more detail of the further funding provided by Gramercy, including, importantly, the difference between the 14 Aug 2025 $65m tranche (I understand to be used for overheads generally) and the 19 Sept 2025 $30m tranche (ringfenced for Pan NOx). It is important that Alicia explains in her statement that the $30m is so ringfenced, and ideally how that has been achieved.&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Second, given Martyn’s statement about the PG case leads resigning, &nbsp;Section IV [14.4] of Alicia’s WS needs fleshing out. At present I find this para a little hard to follow. Ideally Alicia needs to explain when the case leads resigned, why they did, and when their notice period ends (and if this is after the conclusion of the evidence in the PDD trial).&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Third, it is very likely that Ben or one of the other KCs will be asked at the PTR about the circumstances of Peter’s resignation, what precisely he has alleged and why it is wrong. I understand you will be limited in what you can say, but if you can go further than what is in the WS, it would be a good idea to do so. At the very least Alicia needs to state what has already been said in correspondence: that there is a dispute with Peter.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp